---
description: Enforce production-grade Capacitor implementation patterns across architecture, native sync, and release hygiene
alwaysApply: true
---

capacitor-core-practices:

- Keep `@capacitor/core`, `@capacitor/cli`, `@capacitor/android`, and `@capacitor/ios` on aligned majors.
- After installing, removing, or upgrading native plugins, always run platform sync before testing.
- Prefer `capacitor.config.ts` for environment-aware config and release-safe defaults.
- Never leave development server URLs or cleartext transport enabled for production builds.
- Check plugin availability and platform capability before invoking native APIs.
- Separate web-layer and native-layer impact in every implementation summary.
- Document whether each change is OTA-eligible or requires app-store release.
- Avoid heavy app startup work on the main thread; keep boot path stable for update health checks.
- Use explicit fallback paths for unavailable permissions/devices/plugins.
- Require deterministic release notes: changed files, migration steps, rollback target.
- Treat changes to config, entitlements, manifests, and native code as store-release scope.
- Include project-native verification commands (lint, tests, build, sync, release checks).
